<setup>

  <selectFromSequence name="k" from="2" to="5" step="1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="B" from="15" to="25" step="5"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="S" from="8" to="12" step="2"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="Vol" from="30" to="45" step="5"/>

  <selectFromSequence name="p" from="0.5" to="1.5" step="0.5"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="q" from="4" to="5" step="1"/>


  <math name="volEq2">$Vol/($k*w^2)</math>
  <math name="volEq3">$Vol/$k * 1/w^2</math>
  <math name="costEq">$B*$k*w^2 + 2*$S*($k+1)*w*h</math>

  <function name="costFxn" variable="w">$B*$k*w^2 + $S*2*($k+1)*$Vol/($k*w)</function>
  <function name="CP" variable="w">2*$B*$k*w - $S*2*($k+1)*$Vol/($k*w^2)</function>
  <function name="H" variable="w">$Vol/($k*w^2)</function>

  <number name="crNum">($S*($k+1)*$Vol/($B*$k^2))^(1/3)</number>

  <number name="absMin">$$costFxn($crNum)</number>
  <number name="hMin">$$H($crNum)</number>
  <number name="leftMax">$$costFxn($p)</number>
  <number name="rightMax">$$costFxn($q)</number>
  <number name="hLeft">$$H($p)</number>
  <number name="hRight">$$H($q)</number>

</setup>

<p>
  An open rectangular storage container is being built to the following specifications:
  <ul>
    <li>
      <p>
        the length of its base is <m>$k</m> times the width of the base;
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        the materials for the base cost $<m>$B</m> per square meter;
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        the materials for the sides cost $<m>$S</m> per square meter;
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        the storage container should hold <m>$Vol</m> cubic meters of volume
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        the smallest allowable width of the container is <m>w = $p</m> meters, and the largest allowable width is <m>w = $q</m> meters.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
  Our goal is to find the dimensions of the storage container that produce the absolute minimum and absolute maximum cost.
</p>

<p>
  Draw two possible pictures of the container.  Label the shortest base side <m>w</m>, the longer base side <m>\ell</m>, and the height <m>h</m>.
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        Based on the given information, a key relationship between <m>\ell</m> and <m>w</m> is that <answer><label><m>\ell = </m></label>$k*w</answer>.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        State a formula for the volume of the container that involves only the variables <m>w</m> and <m>h</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer><label><m>V=</m></label>$k*w^2*h</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        State a formula for the cost of the container that involves only the variables <m>w</m> and <m>h</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer><label><m>C=</m></label>$B*$k*w^2 + 2*$S*($k+1)*w*h</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Use the constraint (that volume is fixed) to find an equation that relates the variables <m>w</m> and <m>h</m>, and solve that equation for <m>h</m>.  State that equation in the provided space below.
      </p>
      <p>
         <answer simplifyOnCompare symbolicEquality><mathInput name="constraintEq">
           <label><m>h = </m></label>
         </mathInput>
           <award><when>$constraintEq = $volEq2 or $constraintEq = $volEq3</when></award>
         </answer>
      </p>
      <!--
      <p>
        VolEq: <m>$volEq</m>
      </p>
      -->
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Use the contraint equation appropriately to find a formula for the container's cost that depends only on <m>w</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer simplifyOnCompare symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
          <mathInput name="costEntered">
            <label><m>C(w)=</m></label>
          </mathInput>
          <award><when>$costEntered=$costFxn</when></award>
        </answer>
      </p>
      <!--
      <p>
        <m>C(w)= $costFxn</m>
      </p>
      -->
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Find <m>C'(w)</m> and then find all critical numbers of <m>C</m> that lie in the domain of interest: <m>$p \le w \le $q</m>.  If there's more than one such critical number, separate them with commas; if there are no such critical numbers, enter <em>none</em>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute name="CPEntered"><label><m>C'(w) = </m></label>$CP</answer>
      </p>
      <p>
        The critical number(s) within the domain are <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label><m>w = </m></label>$crNum</answer>
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Finally, find the absolute maximum and absolute minimum possible cost of the container, along with the dimensions of the container that achieve those respective costs.
      </p>
      <p>
        The absolute minimum cost of the container is
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
          <label><m>C = </m></label>$absMin</answer>
        dollars and this absolute minimum is achieved when the container has dimensions
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label><m>w = </m></label>$crNum</answer>,
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label><m>\ell = </m></label>$k*$crNum</answer>,
        and <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><label><m>h = </m></label>$hMin</answer>.
      </p>

      <p>
        The absolute maximum cost of the container is
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
          <mathInput name="vMaxEntered">
            <label><m>C = </m></label>
          </mathInput>
          <award><when>
            ($vMaxEntered=$leftMax and $leftMax >= $rightMax) or ($vMaxEntered=$rightMax and $rightMax >= $leftMax)
          </when></award></answer>
        dollars and this absolute maximum is achieved when the container has dimensions
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
          <mathInput name="wMax">
            <label><m>w = </m></label>
          </mathInput>
          <award><when>
            ($wMax=$q and $leftMax <= $rightMax) or ($wMax=$p and $rightMax <= $leftMax)
          </when></award></answer>,
          <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
            <mathInput name="lMax">
              <label>
                <m>\ell = </m>
              </label>
            </mathInput>
            <award><when>
            ($lMax=$k*$q and $leftMax <= $rightMax) or ($lMax=$k*$p and $rightMax <= $leftMax)
          </when></award>
          </answer>,
        and 
        <answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.01" allowedErrorIsAbsolute>
          <mathInput name="hMax">
            <label><m>h = </m></label>
          </mathInput>
          <award><when>
            ($hMax=$hRight and $leftMax <= $rightMax) or ($hMax=$hLeft and $rightMax <= $leftMax)
          </when></award></answer>.
      </p>

    </li>
  </ol>
</p>


<!-- testing

      <p>
        vFxn: <m>$vFxn</m>, volumeEntered: <m>$volumeEntered</m>, costEq = <m>$costEq</m>, vPrime=<m>$VP</m>, vpEntered: <m>$vPEntered</m>
        </p>
450=60w^2+96wh
\frac{3w^2\left(450-60w^2\right)}{96w}

      <p>
        crNum=$crNum, absMax=$absMax, hMax=$hMax
      </p>

-->
